# Paper 1 current manuscript

Target journal: **Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery (DMKD)**.
Title: **Source-Grounded Constraint Validation for Document-Level Knowledge Graph Repair**.

Entry point: `paper1/main.tex`. The local compiled PDF is `paper1/main.pdf`
(ignored by Git). The current revision uses shorter sentences and reports
results directly; scope and limitations are grouped in one subsection.

## Current evidence

The 2026-09-23 follow-up uses 20 development receipts and 60 new test receipts,
with code/scoring frozen before test inference. See
`exps/paper1_receipt_followup/README.md`. It tests a field-evidence index against
a simple pipeline sharing the same field definitions and source lines.


- Controlled and actual extraction errors on Chinese record texts:
  `exps/paper1_repair_benchmark/`, `exps/paper1_submission_extensions/`.
- Matched Gemma contexts, shared-response filtering, and actual sequential
  selection traces: `exps/paper1_mechanism_audit/`.
- Independent SROIE receipt transcripts with upstream human field labels:
  `exps/paper1_external_receipts/`.
- Two-person review files and detailed Chinese instructions:
  `exps/paper1_human_review/README.md`.

New experiments use Gemma. Previously stored Claude predictions are reused
without new Claude calls. The Chinese record source-copy baseline remains
visible at 100%; external receipt results are reported separately. The
sequential selector is a comparison, not the source of the 98% pipeline result.
The execution audit is retained in `docs/audits/paper1_method_implementation_audit.md`.

## Real human review

Give each person only their own ZIP under
`exps/paper1_human_review/delivery/`. Each contains 200 input-discrepancy items,
200 actual-edit items, an offline HTML form, XLSX, and instructions. Keep the
coordinator package private from annotators. Labels are blank until real
annotators complete them. Existing SROIE human annotations and this pending
independent review are distinct sources of evidence.

## Build

```bash
python3 exps/paper1_mechanism_audit/write_paper_tables.py
python3 paper1/make_submission_figures.py
python3 paper1/make_audit_figures.py
python3 exps/paper1_external_receipts/analyze.py
python3 exps/paper1_external_receipts/whitespace_check.py
python3 exps/paper1_external_receipts/write_paper.py
python3 exps/paper1_receipt_followup/write_paper.py
cd paper1
tectonic -X compile main.tex --keep-logs
```

Receipt generators update their sections and figures from completed result
archives. Run the follow-up generator last: it writes the current abstract
and conclusion. All active figures are vector PDFs with
embedded Times New Roman. Original diagrams and historical result files are
retained for traceability. Reference sources are documented in
`docs/audits/paper1_reference_sources.json`; the added SROIE citation was checked
against Crossref DOI metadata (ICDAR 2019, pp. 1516–1520).
